Why, oh why, is my 3-window setup of Amiga NetHack 3.1.3
flashing after every character move, whenever the 3 screens
overlap?! This setup makes the game unplayable, and I've had to
go back to 3.1.2.  Not everyone is running in PAL, you know, and
in non-laced NTSC it just won't all fit without overlap, even
with overscan!	:-(

It's a real neat idea to have one window each for the messages,
one for the map, and one for stats, but for every move each
window flashes active for a fraction of a second, and on a stock
68000 it is visually unbearable.

Any help via email would be greatly appreciated, as no one in
comp.sys.amiga.games has ever replied to my two postings on this.
Arrrgh!

